## ISS-009: Browser extension content script matches all URLs

### File
`/root/Redball/browser-extension/manifest.json`

### Original
```json
  "content_scripts": [
    {
      "matches": ["<all_urls>"],
      "js": ["content.js"],
      "run_at": "document_idle"
    }
  ],
```

### Replacement
```json
  "content_scripts": [
    {
      "matches": ["http://localhost:5000/*"],
      "js": ["content.js"],
      "run_at": "document_idle"
    }
  ],
```

### Original (web_accessible_resources)
```json
  "web_accessible_resources": [
    {
      "resources": ["injected.js"],
      "matches": ["<all_urls>"]
    }
  ]
```

### Replacement
```json
  "web_accessible_resources": [
    {
      "resources": ["injected.js"],
      "matches": ["http://localhost:5000/*"]
    }
  ]
```

### Reason
Narrows the content script and web-accessible resource scope from every page to the local Redball API, reducing privacy exposure and store-review risk.

### Verification
Load extension in a browser and confirm the content script is only injected on `http://localhost:5000/*`.
